Not a real file to add as-is — this is a diff note for the registration
entry that must be added to the upstream file
toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs (verified present at this path in
the pinned ESR 140.0.5 tree, target/gecko-src/gecko-dev/).

That file exports a single big object literal (JSWINDOWACTORS, consumed by
ActorManagerParent.addJSWindowActors()) with one entry per registered actor
pair — see the real "WebChannel" and "ViewSourcePage" entries already in
that file for the two closest precedents (generic page<->chrome channel,
and a custom-scheme `matches` pattern), both read directly from the pinned
tree while writing this scaffold.

Add a new entry (exact insertion point: anywhere in the JSWINDOWACTORS
object literal, alphabetical-ish ordering is followed loosely by the
existing file but not strictly enforced):

    PyxisBridge: {
      parent: {
        esModuleURI: "resource://gre/actors/PyxisBridgeParent.sys.mjs",
      },
      child: {
        esModuleURI: "resource://gre/actors/PyxisBridgeChild.sys.mjs",
        // REAL BUG, found via a real boot (2026-07-06): without an `events`
        // block here, `matches`/`allFrames` alone only gate an explicit
        // `getActor()` call — they do NOT cause the actor to be created
        // automatically. Nothing in this codebase ever calls
        // `windowGlobal.getActor("PyxisBridge")` (window.geckoOS is meant to
        // just be present, unconditionally), so the actor pair was NEVER
        // instantiated for any pyxis:// document at all — confirmed by
        // temporarily adding console.error to both PyxisBridgeChild's and
        // PyxisBridgeParent's actorCreated() and observing neither ever
        // fired, even though the document itself demonstrably loaded (a
        // separate fprintf canary in PyxisProtocolHandler::NewChannel showed
        // pyxis://bloom/index.html + its JS/CSS/favicon all being fetched
        // normally). Real precedent for the fix, read directly from this
        // same file: AboutTranslations uses exactly this
        // `events: { DOMDocElementInserted: {} }` block under `child` to
        // "run the actor before any content of the page appears to inject
        // functions" — the identical requirement PyxisBridge has.
        events: {
          DOMDocElementInserted: {},
        },
      },

      // Match every pyxis:// page, at document-start, in every frame —
      // app content can embed pyxis:// iframes of the SAME app (cross-app
      // iframes are cross-origin per PyxisProtocolHandler's design and
      // would get their own actor instance anyway, which is correct: each
      // origin's bridge call is independently capability-checked against
      // that origin's own app-id, see PyxisBridgeParent.sys.mjs's
      // _appIdForThisActor()).
      matches: ["pyxis://*/*"],
      allFrames: true,
    },

Also required, and CONFIRMED against the real file (toolkit/actors/moz.build
in the pinned tree, verified directly this session): every actor .sys.mjs
under toolkit/actors/ is listed in a `FINAL_TARGET_FILES.actors += [...]`
block, which is what maps these source files to resource://gre/actors/*.sys.mjs
URLs at build time. Real excerpt from the pinned tree:

    FINAL_TARGET_FILES.actors += [
        "AboutHttpsOnlyErrorChild.sys.mjs",
        "AboutHttpsOnlyErrorParent.sys.mjs",
        "AudioPlaybackChild.sys.mjs",
        "AudioPlaybackParent.sys.mjs",
        ... (alphabetical) ...
    ]

Add, in alphabetical position:

    "PyxisBridgeChild.sys.mjs",
    "PyxisBridgeParent.sys.mjs",

Apply by placing gecko/patches/pyxis/toolkit/actors/PyxisBridgeChild.sys.mjs
and PyxisBridgeParent.sys.mjs into toolkit/actors/ in the real checkout, and
adding both filenames to the FINAL_TARGET_FILES.actors list in
toolkit/actors/moz.build at the correct alphabetical position. Confirmed by
direct inspection of the pinned tree's real ordering around there:

    "PrintingSelectionChild.sys.mjs",
    "PurgeSessionHistoryChild.sys.mjs",
    "RemotePageChild.sys.mjs",

"PyxisBridgeChild.sys.mjs" / "PyxisBridgeParent.sys.mjs" sort between
"PurgeSessionHistoryChild.sys.mjs" and "RemotePageChild.sys.mjs" — insert
there.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
The unified diff below is generated from the checkout and is applied with
  git apply gecko/patches/pyxis/<path>.PYXIS_DIFF
(or `patch -p1 <`). Everything above this line is rationale, not content;
git apply ignores it. Regenerate with scripts/regen-gecko-patches.sh.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

diff --git a/toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs b/toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs
index 975188ded7d8..f2e9b4d83588 100644
--- a/toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs
@@ -555,6 +555,49 @@ let JSWINDOWACTORS = {
     allFrames: true,
   },
 
+  PyxisBridge: {
+    parent: {
+      esModuleURI: "resource://gre/actors/PyxisBridgeParent.sys.mjs",
+    },
+    child: {
+      esModuleURI: "resource://gre/actors/PyxisBridgeChild.sys.mjs",
+      // REAL BUG, found via a real boot (2026-07-06): `matches`/`allFrames`
+      // alone only gate an explicit `getActor()` call — they do NOT cause
+      // the actor to be created automatically. Since nothing in this
+      // codebase ever calls `windowGlobal.getActor("PyxisBridge")`
+      // (window.geckoOS is meant to just be present, unconditionally, with
+      // no page code having to ask for it first), the actor pair was NEVER
+      // being instantiated at all for any pyxis:// document — confirmed by
+      // adding a console.error to both PyxisBridgeChild's and
+      // PyxisBridgeParent's actorCreated() and observing neither ever
+      // fired, even though the document itself demonstrably loaded (a
+      // separate fprintf canary in PyxisProtocolHandler::NewChannel showed
+      // pyxis://bloom/index.html + its JS/CSS/favicon all being fetched
+      // normally). Real precedent for the fix, read directly from this same
+      // file: AboutTranslations (above) uses exactly this
+      // `events: { DOMDocElementInserted: {} }` block under `child` to
+      // "run the actor before any content of the page appears to inject
+      // functions" — the identical requirement PyxisBridge has. Without
+      // this, every EchoClient.callMethod() call silently fell through to
+      // the mock backend forever (window.geckoOS was simply undefined),
+      // regardless of any other fix already made (initialized: true,
+      // Echo transport, capability gating, etc. all execute correctly —
+      // they just never ran, because the child actor never existed).
+      events: {
+        DOMDocElementInserted: {},
+      },
+    },
+
+    // Match every pyxis:// page, at document-start, in every frame — app
+    // content can embed pyxis:// iframes of the SAME app (cross-app iframes
+    // are cross-origin per PyxisProtocolHandler's design and get their own
+    // actor instance anyway, independently capability-checked against that
+    // origin's own app-id; see PyxisBridgeParent.sys.mjs's
+    // _appIdForThisActor()).
+    matches: ["pyxis://*/*"],
+    allFrames: true,
+  },
+
   ReportBrokenSite: {
     parent: {
       esModuleURI: "resource://gre/actors/ReportBrokenSiteParent.sys.mjs",
